; Interrupting a waiting process whose stack group holds a register of all
; ones.  The microcode sets a register to all ones (SETO: M-K in %DRAW-CHAR
; and the transporter, M-E), and a stack group switch saves it so in the
; stack group's leader: data type 77, no data type.  EH::SG-SAVE-STATE, run by
; a process interrupt (sys/sys2/proces.lisp), took every code but a few as a
; pointer (SI:%POINTER-TYPE-P, sys/sys2/lmmac.lisp) and followed this one to
; address 37777777777, past the 28-bit space: the machine halted, as when a
; TELNET session ended.  A code past DTP-CHARACTER is now no pointer.  Run with
; --compile --files sys/sys2/lmmac.lisp,sys/eh/eh.lisp (the defsubst is
; compiled into SG-SAVE-STATE).  The first three cases are controls.
(si:%pointer-type-p dtp-list) => T
(si:%pointer-type-p dtp-fix) => NIL
(progn (defvar *pi-p* nil) (setq *pi-p* (process-run-function "pi wait" #'(lambda () (process-wait "Forever" #'false)))) (process-sleep 30) (process-whostate *pi-p*)) => "Forever"
(si:%pointer-type-p #o77) => NIL
(si:%pointer-type-p (1+ dtp-character)) => NIL
(progn (%p-store-tag-and-pointer (locf (si:sg-ac-k (process-stack-group *pi-p*))) #o377 -1) (%p-ldb #o4010 (locf (si:sg-ac-k (process-stack-group *pi-p*))))) => 255
(progn (defvar *pi-ran* nil) (send *pi-p* :interrupt #'(lambda () (setq *pi-ran* t))) (process-sleep 60) *pi-ran*) => T
(progn (send *pi-p* :kill) t) => T
